  "certified_type": {
    "category": "Non-automatic weighing instrument",
    "type_designations": ["DPS-700", "CM-700"],
    "module_designation": "Digital indicator",
    "description": "This instrument utilises either the digital indicating device designated the DPS-700 indicator with optional labeller, or its compact version designated the CM-700, connected to a weighing platform to form a Class III or IIIII, mains-powered, self-indicating non-automatic weighing instrument. Main features: processor and converter unit comprising a Teraoka TPB-2930 CPU and a Teraoka TPB-2786 A/D converter; touch screen (colour TFT-LCD module); optional labeller type Digi DPS 700 thermal printer; metallic supporting frame (DPS-700 only). Devices: initial zero setting, semi-automatic zero setting, zero tracking, semi-automatic subtractive tare weighing, determination of stability of equilibrium, indication of stability of equilibrium, zero indicator, PLUs, preset tare, price calculation. Load cell: any compatible load cell may be used provided it has a valid OIML R60 Certificate of Conformity containing the load cell types and data required for the manufacturer's declaration of compatibility of modules; compatibility of load cells and indicator is established by the manufacturer by means of the compatibility of modules calculation; a load cell marked NH is allowed only if humidity testing to R76 has been conducted. Interfaces: load cell 4- or 6-wire connection, Ethernet, USB, keyboard. Software: version number 2.xx.xx.xxxx displayed during power-up; the legal metrological code is contained in DPS700.dll protected by a checksum; alternatively the instrument may use the World View software with HeaderDisplay.dll (Version 1.0.0.10) and DPS710.dll (Version 1.0.0.29); direct sales to the public are permitted when using the World View software."
  },
